Generate shell completions.

The script is written to stdout and covers the commands this build has. `-q` has no effect: the script is the answer.

Usage: evnx completions [OPTIONS] <SHELL>

Arguments:
  <SHELL>
          The shell to write the script for, in any case
          
          [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

Options:
      --no-color
          Disable colored output

  -q, --quiet
          Print nothing on success. Findings, warnings, errors and requested data still print

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Install, for the shell you use (create the folder first if it does not exist),
then open a new shell:
  bash        evnx completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/evnx
  zsh         evnx completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_evnx
              and in ~/.zshrc, before compinit: fpath=(~/.zfunc $fpath)
  fish        evnx completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/evnx.fish
  powershell  evnx completions powershell >> $PROFILE
  elvish      evnx completions elvish >> ~/.config/elvish/rc.elv

The script lists this build's commands: generate it again after an upgrade.

Exit codes:
    0  Ran, nothing to report
    2  Could not run: usage, config, I/O, or refused before any change
  141  Output closed early (broken pipe)

Full guide: https://docs.evnx.dev/cli/commands/completions
